DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270312
SUMMARY:GDL
DESCRIPTION:Runtime: 216 minutes\nRating: 0.0\nGenres: Drama\, Comedy\n\nGDL is a Mexican dark comedy-drama film set in Guadalajara. We meet Daniel Lurdez\, a young man who\, after arriving in the city\, ends up in a psychologist’s office. Seeing that he is clearly struggling\, she asks him\, “Why do you feel like you feel this way?” Daniel begins to tell his story\, and through his memories\, we experience his first year in Guadalajara: the people he met\, his relationships\, parties\, hopes\, disappointments\, and failures. Throughout this year\, we discover a gigantic\, contradictory\, and vibrant city; a monster that slowly transforms everyone who arrives. Guadalajara promises opportunities and a new life\, but it can also destroy the dreams of those trying to find their place in it. Daniel arrived looking to become someone different. In the end\, the city turned him into someone he never imagined he would become. GODS\, DEVILS AND LIARS.\n\nTrailer: 
END:VEVENT

